### Page 5 of 16

```text
UDC-22-00248-02
September 6, 2022
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to approve the Lake Minnehaha III Expedited Preliminary Plat, advancing the Final Plat to the
Governing Body.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

UDC 2.1.2 Preliminary Plat Approval

UDC 2.1.3 Final Plat Approval

UDC Article 4 Subdivisions

UDC Article 5 Zoning Regulations

PlanCheyenne

BACKGROUND:

The applicant is requesting approval of a plat to separate two houses on one lot into two individually sellable
properties. It is Staff s understanding the properties already have completely separate utilities and addresses.
The NR-2 zone allows the smallest type of single family detached housing, therefore the property is going
through a concurrent zone change. The lots also do not meet a few standards as currently developed. As
such, the lots have received variances to allow the existing conditions to continue with the new lot line
should the properties be raised, new development would be required to meet standards or receive new
variances.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

ANALYSIS OF APPLICATION CONFORMANCE WITH REVIEW CRITERIA:

Should the Planning Commission wish to recommend approval of the Preliminary Plat, the Commission
must make the following findings required in UDC 2.1.2.d   a detailed analysis is below:

1) The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan. (UDC 2.1.2.d.1)

The future land use map within PlanCheyenne identifies this area as developing with a mix of
residential development, and the proposed plat in this zoning district would be compatible with
this objective. PlanCheyenne supports the use of existing infrastructure and timely provision of

