### Page 6 of 16

```text
UDC-22-00248-02
September 6, 2022
services (including emergency and education services). This development is proposed in an area
which has largely existing infrastructure and no expansion of infrastructure is necessary. This
development is in conformance with the principles and future land uses identified in
PlanCheyenne. The property is within the Urban Service Boundary and has access to all utilities.

The application complies with this review criterion.

2) The application reflects sound planning and urban design principles with respect to existing
and potential future development in the vicinity, including consideration of current and future
streets, open spaces, blocks and lots, and public utilities or facilities. (UDC 2.1.2.d.2)

The proposed application is adding a property line on an existing block. The surrounding area is
largely previously developed and this would be considered an infill project. Reutilizing properties
for infill development is an important urban planning principle, and the proposed plat would not
have an undue influence on the surrounding properties. The built form is not anticipated to
change, the only difference is that the two houses will be under separate ownership.

The application complies with this review criterion.

3) The division of land meets the purposes, intent, and all applicable standards in Article 4. (UDC
2.1.2.d.3)

Community Facility Fees (4.2):
Subdivisions which do not increase the total number of lots are exempt from plat fees, and
this property was originally platted in 1890 with two lots (the original lots are skinny lots
extending all the way north and south). This plat is essentially reconfiguring the two lots and
is exempt from these fees.

Transportation Network (4.3):
This plat is occurring within an area of the community which has been previously developed.
The existing block and street network largely meet applicable standards.

Open Space (4.4):
Open space is required at 750sqft per unit or 8% of the gross development area, whichever
is less. However, due to the size of the property, plat-level open space is not required.

Required Improvements (4.5):
This plat appears to be able to provide all required utilities to the lots within this
development.

Public Safety Fees (4.6):
The applicant proposes to upgrade the existing space, therefore, it is anticipated that the
remodel on the property will qualify for an exception from this fee.

The application complies with this review criterion.
```

